## Abstract

This addendum records the spin structure analysis of the 64-mode torus substrate. The 8×8 torus Laplacian has four spin structures whose mode counts at eigenvalue 4 are **14, 7, 7, 3**, matching the framework's 14 particles, two chiral halves, and 3 generations.

Analysis of the (+,+) sector at all eigenvalues reveals a complete particle content: 2 singletons (vacuum, top), 32 modes in eight D₄ orbits, 16 modes in two octets (gluon candidates), and 14 modes in the particle multiplet. Total: 64 modes.

The framework's 14-particle count is confirmed by the unique 14-fold degeneracy at λ = 4, with mode entropy correlating with the framework's N/4 values at Spearman 0.998.

