## 7. The Hidden Modes (Mixed Sectors)

The mixed sectors (+,−) and (−,+) contribute 14 modes at λ = 4; the (−,−) sector contributes 3. Total hidden modes: 17.

The top 14 modes by entropy across all sectors are drawn from all four sectors:

- 10 from (+,+)
- 3 from (−,+)
- 1 from (+,−)
- 0 from (−,−)

Their entropy ordering matches the framework's N/4 ordering at Spearman 0.998, but the specific selection differs from the (+,+)-only assignment (W, Z, H, t fall below the top 14 cutoff).

The 8 particles with near-exact hidden partners (entropy difference < 0.01) are: dark photon, top, bottom, Higgs, W, charm, tau, Z. All have N/4 < 14.

The 6 particles without hidden partners are: up, down, strange, electron, muon, neutrino. All have N/4 ≥ 14.

**Interpretation:** the hidden modes have their own entropy range (2.14 to 2.55), below the particle range (2.43 to 2.64). Only particles whose entropy falls within the hidden range have exact mirrors.

